# Trivy ignore file — read by aquasecurity/trivy-action (image + fs scans) by
# default. Every entry here is a SECURITY FINDING WE HAVE ASSESSED AND ACCEPTED,
# with a written justification + a re-review trigger. This is NOT a place to
# silence real exposure — a permanently-red Security Gate trains everyone to
# ignore it, so we keep the gate GREEN and document each exception here instead.
# Review this file whenever the base image / npm is bumped.

# ── CVE-2026-12151 — undici DoS via unbounded WebSocket-frame memory growth ──
# Affected: undici 6.26.0 BUNDLED INSIDE THE npm CLI
#   (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/undici) shipped in
#   node:22.23.1-slim. Fixed in undici 6.27.0 / 7.28.0 / 8.5.0.
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • This is npm's OWN vendored undici, NOT our application's. Our app's undici
#     is pinned to ^7.28.0 (patched) via package.json `overrides`.
#   • npm IS invoked at runtime, narrowly (corrected 2026-08-31): the daily
#     immune job spawns `npm audit --json` (npmWatch.ts:273) and
#     codebaseMonitor execs `npm outdated --json` — both talk only to the
#     npm registry. The DoS requires an attacker-controlled WebSocket peer
#     talking to undici, which neither invocation exposes.
#   • The latest Node 22 LTS (22.23.1) still bundles this npm/undici, and npm
#     vendors undici transitively (no clean version-pin fix); upgrading global
#     npm in the image is unverifiable pre-build and churns the toolchain.
# Re-review trigger: drop this line once a node:22-slim ships an npm whose
# bundled undici is >= 6.27.0 (then the bump alone clears it).
CVE-2026-12151

# ── CVE-2026-14257 — brace-expansion ReDoS ──────────────────────────────────
# Affected: brace-expansion 5.0.7 BUNDLED INSIDE the npm CLI installed by the
#   Dockerfile's `npm install -g npm@latest` (the refresh that exists to chase
#   exactly this class — npm's own bundle now trails its fix).
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • The APP's copies are patched (1.1.18 / 2.1.4 / 5.0.9 in the lockfile;
#     verified across every instance).
#   • npm runs at runtime only as `npm audit` / `npm outdated` subprocesses
#     against registry JSON; the ReDoS needs attacker-supplied glob/brace
#     patterns, which those invocations never take from external input.
# Re-review trigger: drop when `npm install -g npm@latest` pulls a bundle
# with brace-expansion >= 5.0.8 (re-run the container scan after any npm or
# base-image bump).
CVE-2026-14257

# ── CVE-2026-69192 — ip-address parsing flaw ────────────────────────────────
# Affected: ip-address 10.2.0 BUNDLED INSIDE the npm CLI (same global
#   npm@latest as above). Fixed in 10.3.1.
# Assessment — EXPOSURE NIL:
#   • The APP's ip-address is 10.7.0 (patched) in the lockfile.
#   • Reachable only through npm's registry/proxy plumbing in the two
#     runtime subprocess calls above; no attacker-controlled address strings
#     flow into them.
# Re-review trigger: same as CVE-2026-14257 — clears on npm's next bundle
# refresh.
CVE-2026-69192
